    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in Piedmont in May 1880, marking the town’s early communication hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piedmont%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Piedmont began as a stop on the St. Louis–San Francisco Railroad, fueling its early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://legendsofkansas.com/piedmont-kansas/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Soon after its founding, Piedmont became the region’s main shipping hub, moving grain, livestock, and other farm goods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://legendsofkansas.com/piedmont-kansas/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Over time, Piedmont’s growth stalled, leaving it today largely a ghost town with only a handful of residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://legendsofkansas.com/piedmont-kansas/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Today, Piedmont’s schools and shops have closed, yet it still hosts a post office, a Methodist church, and a small community.",
